    89	## 3. Presentations
    90	
    91	All presentations are Wirtinger presentations of closed braids, with the Zariski--van Kampen convention of the one-node packet: individual affine braid factors impose their Artin action on fibre meridians; the boundary braid is their product and imposes only the product action. A colouring of `G_aff` is a colouring of `G_infinity` that additionally satisfies the affine factors.
    92	
    93	Artin action, same convention as the genus-ladder compiler: `sigma_i` sends `(..., x_i, x_{i+1}, ...)` to `(..., x_i x_{i+1} x_i^{-1}, x_i, ...)`. Negative generators use the inverse automorphism. A transposition colouring is a tuple of transpositions fixed by the word.
